      variant 3 create-unnamed
        summary  `--create` is given without a session name
      variant 4 config-join-and-create
        summary  the workspace's `config.tel` names both a session to join and one to create
    error 2 unserved
      summary  A REPL server could not serve; a failure on account of a coded error carries that error's code
      source src/client/flame_client.scala
      variant 1 port-unavailable
        summary  the TCP port cannot be bound
      variant 2 failed
        summary  serving on the TCP port raised an error
      variant 3 socket-in-use
        summary  the UNIX domain socket is already in use
      variant 4 socket-failed
        summary  serving on the UNIX domain socket raised an error
    error 3 invalid-argument
      summary  A command-line argument is invalid
      source src/client/flame_client.scala
      variant 1 port
        summary  the port is not a valid TCP port
      variant 2 host-missing
        summary  `--host` is given without a hostname
      variant 3 host
        summary  the hostname is not valid
    error 4 unreachable
      summary  The client could not reach a REPL server
      source src/client/flame_client.scala
      variant 1 remote
        summary  the server on the remote host and port refuses the connection
      variant 2 socket
        summary  the server on the UNIX domain socket refuses the connection
      variant 3 launch
        summary  a REPL server could not be started in the background
    error 5 several-servers
      summary  Several local REPL servers are running, and the client cannot choose between them
      source src/client/flame_client.scala
    error 6 terminal
      summary  The terminal could not be initialised; the failure carries the terminal error's code
      source src/client/flame_client.scala
  subdivision 20 flame-launcher

